Theorem 5.1, abstraction case (Scott 1981, PRG-19), states that the map recovered from the curry of an approximable map g at a context element v, applied at x, equals g at the pair of v and x. Theorem 5.1, application case (Scott 1981, PRG-19), states that evaluation composed with the pairing of two approximable maps F and G sends w to the map of F at w applied to the value of G at w. Theorem 5.1, constant case (Scott 1981, PRG-19), states that the constant map with value k sends every element to k. Theorem 5.1, tuple case (Scott 1981, PRG-19), states that the pairing of two approximable maps sends an element to the pair of their values at that element. Theorem 5.1, variable case (Scott 1981, PRG-19), states that the first projection sends the pair of x and y to x.

The numbered name theorem_51 is the conjunction of these statements. The proof is that conjunction.
